    "reviewed_findings": [
      "The final main page and three implementation pages match the three actual trait IDs and six bound marks. Weapon labels and reverse index entries match the canonical associations; UI verification reports six bindings and no outside exact items.",
      "The own-tier proof supports I–IV movement_speed values .17/.18/.19/.20, +17% through +20% formatting, and a 2-second duration for each of the three implementations. Each wrapper has one direct clone of the shared activation buff, with no additional wrapper assignment found.",
      "The trigger description matches the weapon-special activation event. The six actual model action tables do not allow reactivation while special state remains active; the event guard also requires the 0.5-second interval. Ordinary attacks, special attack hits, and subsequent chainsaw hits are not the activation event.",
      "First-effect wording correctly places ProcBuff event handling before stat-cache rebuild. A later qualifying activation refreshes the same 2-second timer without stacking; switching away suppresses the held-slot contribution while time continues, and unequipping removes the trait effect.",
      "The movement-speed calculation distinguishes additive value h from other additive value q and fixed multiplier m. The worked example is arithmetically correct: (1+0.25+0.20)/(1+0.25)-1 = 16%; sprint has a separate multiplier, so the trait does not promise a fixed final-speed increase.",
      "The RAW keys and paired English/Traditional Chinese source hash match the RAW receipt. All four tier reconstructions use the exact formatter prefix and duration; omitted runtime conditions are labeled as not covered rather than translation contradictions.",
      "The generic weapon_trait_200 icon and chainsword weapon_trait_079 icon are represented by separate verified attachment receipts and correspond to the formal image links and reverse weapon pages."
    ],
